    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238-a1">

                <pb facs="0367" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg279"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dawson to Mr.
                            Sanchez.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August 29,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: By the award rendered on the 14th
                    day of July, 1904, by the commission of arbitration under the protocol of
                    January 31, 1903, between my <pb facs="0368" n="280" xml:id="pg280"/> Government
                    and that of this Republic, it was provided that the United States should appoint
                    a financial agent to collect the sum due under the award.</p>
                <p>Pursuant to instructions from the Department of State I now have the honor to
                    inform you that Mr. John T. Abbott has been appointed as financial agent under
                    the provisions of the award in question.</p>
                <p>I improve the opportunity to renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Dawson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
